Cap the localised edge/face search in IntTools_BeanFaceIntersector

Targets OCCT V8_0_1. Introduced in Fillet on 2026-10-25 (744bd00).

Edge/face intersection with a B-spline face of degree > 2 and more than one
span in both directions (what a non-uniform scale makes of a revolve, sphere
or torus) first "localises" candidate (curve range, surface patch) pairs by
box overlap. Every patch box is enlarged by one deflection estimated on the
whole face's coarse knot grid, often several millimetres, so boxes never
shrink and the search returns thousands to hundreds of thousands of
candidates, each followed by a global extremum search. One transversal
crossing took 3.3 s (61 556 candidates).

The patch makes LocalizeSolutions give up once it has collected more than
256 candidates, so ComputeLocalized takes the generic path that OCCT already
uses for every other surface type (and when localisation fails).
Well-behaved localisations are unchanged. Cold evaluate of the benchmark
fixture 81 600 -> 7 815 ms.

